-- Row il-69. EXPECTED RED: three assertions that fail on purpose, two for item I1 and one for item I2.
-- I1 (a): in the literal result of the instruction, every occurrence of the word for "section" is followed by a section number. False: the first occurrence is followed by the first word of the words put in place, which is not a section number.
-- I1 (b): the consolidation's words cite no repealed provision. False: they cite subsection (b) of section 23, which item (8) of SH 2274 repeals.
-- I2: the section cited by section 113d(a)(1) is in force on 2027-01-01 as the instruments read give it. False: the instruments read give section 41 as repealed, with a start bounded by 2016-01-01.
-- The count, three, is declared in check.sh (expected_failed) and in encoding.json (expected_red). If a later instrument changes what one of these reads, its assertion turns green and the declared count must go down with it.
-- These assertions state properties of the printed words and of the statuses; they say nothing about which reading is right, what a court would do, or how any provision should read.

§ `Expected red`

#ASSERT `every occurrence of the word is followed by a section number` "סעיף" (`the literal result of the instruction` `item I1: section 124(a)(4) cites section 23(b)`)
#ASSERT `the words cite no repealed provision` "סעיף" (`item I1: the consolidation text`'s `its words`) `the provisions item I1 can cite`
#ASSERT `the section the reference cites is in force on` `item I2: section 113d(a)(1) cites section 41` (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
